    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced. The bull case rests on strong long-term structure: AAPL holds above the 200-day SMA ($180.01, closing at $183.61), the golden cross is intact, and FY2023 cash generation is exceptional ($110.5B operating cash flow). The bear case rests on deteriorating near-term momentum: price below the 10 EMA ($186.26), 50 SMA ($188.35), and VWMA ($186.55), with MACD swinging from +0.94 to -0.39 and RSI falling to 43.3. Critically, there is zero visibility into the fiscal Q1 2024 earnings catalyst scheduled around this period, which is the single most important near-term factor. With momentum deteriorating while long-term structure holds, and a major catalyst pending with no data, the prudent stance is to maintain the current position rather than force a directional call. Risk-reward is roughly symmetric: downside to $170-175 if the 200 SMA breaks, upside to $186-188 and $194 if support holds.\n\n**Entry Price**: 183.61\n\n**Stop Loss**: 177.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain existing position at current weight; do not add or trim until the earnings catalyst resolves the momentum-versus-structure tension.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
